WEBVTT

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.740
Our deal with those Karafuto 
Ainu men only takes us this far.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.470
Thanks to their sleds, we were 
able to travel a good distance.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:12.280
<b>Shizuka</b>

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.870
But now we're broke.

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:18.910
<i>Sugimoto's idea that Asirpa was still in 
the vicinity of Toyohara was very wrong.</i>

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:23.540
<b>Border</b>

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:23.540
<b>Shizuka</b>

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:23.540
<b>Toyohara</b>

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.560
<i>She'd already gone to Shizuka, 
a town near the border.</i>

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.500
Hey, if we're broke, why don't
 we go hunt some more?

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.340
Some sables!

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:34.080
The streams around here have already frozen,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.930
so catching hoinu is hard.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.610
When the water freezes, 
they can just cross the ice.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.190
What's this thing?

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:21.870
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:27.890
That's a coffin.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:32.020
<b>Episode Twenty-Nine
The Border</b>

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:30.960
What the Uilta call a sky burial.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:32.250
Uilta?

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.920
There are three minority tribes in Karafuto.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:38.880
The Karafuto Ainu.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:49.390
<b>Karafuto Ainu</b>

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:39.990
The Uilta.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:49.390
<b>Uilta</b>

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.340
And the Nivkh.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:49.390
<b>Nivkh</b>

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:45.710
The Karafuto Ainu don't 
live anywhere past Shizuka.

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:48.760
We're now in the territory 
of the Uilta and Nivkh.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:54.110
The only ones who put their coffins in 
trees for a sky burial are the Uilta.

00:02:55.390 --> 00:02:56.820
That's interesting.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.400
That culture is disappearing, though.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:04.450
A lot of the Uilta have been converted, 
and are now buried in the earth.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.660
When your gods change, 
your lifestyle changes, too.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.880
Ogata, what did you shoot?

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.520
An Ezo deer.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.510
There are no Ezo deer in Karafuto.

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:24.510
It resembles a yuk, yes.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.180
But I've never seen anything like it.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.260
That's a reindeer.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.710
It's got something on its neck.

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:32.430
They tie those things to a reindeer's neck

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:35.060
so that they'll collide with 
the legs when it walks,

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.180
keeping them from running.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.190
It's called an ulaa čээngэini.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.650
Let's put it on Shiraishi.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:46.480
Let's line it right up with his dick, 
so he doesn't run off to any brothels.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.570
Ow, ow, ow, ow!

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:51.440
It's a dick čээngэini!

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.580
If it has something around its neck, 
does that mean somebody owns it?

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.470
There should be an Uilta 
settlement around here.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:02.730
They let their reindeer graze at night, 
and then gather them in the morning.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.800
Toh! Toh!

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.260
Toh! Toh!

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.020
That's probably them.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.430
They're calling the reindeer.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.980
Toh! Toh!

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:14.200
Welp, glad I'm not Ogata, 
'cause they're gonna be mad!

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:16.060
Toh! Toh!

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.610
Just apologize.

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.530
Give them some tobacco and they'll be fine.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.440
Toh! Toh!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.730
Ogata, I'll apologize with you.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:20.930
Don't worry.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.120
They live in tents, traveling 
alongside their reindeer herds.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.000
So they don't live in villages?

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.960
Ulaaba waapissaa, ulaaj̈j̈eeri kэrrэurusu.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:46.010
Sundu ulaala anaa biwwuri beejini, sirembe
 waariwappoo bэlэčimэri kэrrэussээrisu.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.720
"If you killed a reindeer, 
you must repay us with a reindeer."

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.360
"If you can't do that, 
help us hunt a wild one."

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.060
They've got so many, 
and they're hunting more?

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.640
The ones they travel with 
are their only wealth.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.620
They never kill and eat them.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:01.530
The only ones they kill and eat 
are the wild mountain reindeer.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:07.740
Asirpa's father once did the same 
thing Ogata did, and shot one.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.640
He did?

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.740
Yeah.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:13.290
In the south of Karafuto, where he lived,

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.010
there are no reindeer.

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:18.440
So he didn't know that 
the Uilta let them graze.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:23.130
He apologized and went on a hunt with them.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:27.880
I've never heard that before, I don't think.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:32.980
Will you go with me, Asirpa?

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:35.830
Yeah.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:38.350
Maybe I'll remember something about Aca.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:51.870
The Uilta call the reindeer they keep "ulaa,"
 and the mountain ones "sire."

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.610
That's a herd of sire.

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:55.830
They're digging in the snow.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.320
There's nutritious "reindeer lichen"
 beneath the snow.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:03.280
And there's always a guard 
watching out for them.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.840
If you shoot him first, the herd will 
be too spooked and confused to run,

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:09.480
which makes it easier to take out the others.

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:12.140
Just like humans, huh?

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:16.140
In order to keep the guard from seeing you,

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.690
you first tie a long rope around your 
own reindeer and make them go ahead.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:23.240
You hide behind it as you get close.

00:06:30.730 --> 00:06:32.570
Oročikku ulaa.

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:35.450
Oročikku ulaa...

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:37.910
How did you know that?

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:41.290
A fake reindeer you use as a 
decoy when you're hunting them.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.940
I just remembered Aca talking about it!

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.220
Ow!

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:51.640
That hurt!

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.640
Are you okay, Shiraishi?

00:06:54.050 --> 00:06:55.790
That hurt!

00:06:55.790 --> 00:07:00.430
If Ogata-chan hadn't shot that reindeer, 
we wouldn't be doing this crap.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:04.380
We should've just run instead of apologizing.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.420
Shiraishi, you're a dick.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.510
No, this is part of the plan.

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:15.160
We needed to make contact with the Uilta 
in order to get any further north.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:19.120
Okay, let's get to reindeer hunting!

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.770
He says the one on the 
right edge is the guard.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.360
Mountain reindeer are 
easily spooked, and hunting them,

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:43.230
even with a gun, is difficult.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.900
Time to hunt.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:51.220
Wait.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:54.920
Tell him I'll shoot first, 
so don't interfere.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.720
Wow!

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.880
Load my gun.

00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:10.440
Give me yours.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.590
A Berdan M1870.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:23.970
It's an old bolt-action rifle,

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:25.230
but not a bad one.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:29.430
Wow!

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.610
He took out the whole herd.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:37.340
If he stays here, there won't
 be any reindeer left.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:40.310
Let's get to work. It's hard to skin them,

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:43.620
and we're going to have to make 
several trips to carry the meat.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:53.010
They say that for some reason, the mountain 
reindeer taste better than the ones you keep.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:59.720
Yup, they've got the same flavor as a yuk!

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.960
Light, with no aftertaste.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.140
Right?

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.310
Do brains ever taste different?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.660
What's she doing?

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:15.500
Churning reindeer milk to make ari.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.900
If it were cow's milk, you'd call it butter.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.370
But this is from a reindeer.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:27.120
When you spread ari on a baked flour 
bread called lipeeskэ, it's delicious.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.820
Hinna! Hinna!

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:36.300
Reindeer milk has a strong, 
sweet flavor! It's hinna!

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:39.210
Their way of life is 
dependent on the reindeer,

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.940
so the foods they eat and 
the houses they live in

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.570
are totally different than the Ainu.

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:43.780
It's really fascinating.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.110
I have a present for you.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.810
A cishpo, an Ainu needle holder.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:53.980
Needles!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:58.940
You've got lots of reindeer pelts, 
so you'll need lots of needles, right?

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.910
Needles are very important to a woman.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:07.830
There's a story of a woman who 
didn't cry when her baby died,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.630
but cried when she lost her needles.

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:13.920
So everything that happened 
today was part of your plan.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:16.700
What was your goal in making 
contact with the Uilta?

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.850
I want to ask your help with something.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.990
All of us have complicated pasts.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:45.960
We can't get the passports 
we need to enter Russia.

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:48.330
So we'll smuggle ourselves in.

00:10:48.730 --> 00:10:51.670
The border region is mostly uninhabited,

00:10:51.670 --> 00:10:56.300
but if we're found by a Japanese or 
Russian patrol, we'll have trouble.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:11:02.450
The nomadic tribes of Karafuto, however, 
are tacitly allowed to travel past the border.

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.390
Which means...

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:08.240
<i>We could disguise ourselves as 
Uilta and cross the border.</i>

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.520
Are we there yet?

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:12.600
Almost!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:16.320
<b>Otaru</b>

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:16.320
The year 1881...

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:23.410
Do you know what happened in the Russian 
capital of St. Petersburg then?

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:32.210
Emperor Alexander II was 
assassinated by a hand-thrown bomb.

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:37.730
The bomb-thrower was part of a 
revolutionary group known as The People's Will.

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:40.990
The members of the group 
were arrested and executed.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:44.060
But one of them remains on the run...

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:48.690
Kiroranke, who was at the 
time a boy in his teens.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:51.550
From one point of view, he's a hero.

00:11:51.550 --> 00:11:54.560
From another, he's a criminal. A regicide.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:12:01.030
So I went ahead and spread some information 
that Russia would be very interested in.

00:12:02.030 --> 00:12:05.130
A revolutionary responsible for 
the emperor's death will be

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:08.740
making his way from Southern 
Karafuto into Russia, very soon.

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:14.410
That's the border marker.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.720
<b>In the 39th year of the Meiji Era</b>

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:26.140
We're past the border!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.850
We're in Russian territory!

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:38.700
Father!

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:39.740
Was he shot?

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.440
Don't stop! Keep going!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:46.030
Ammaa!

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:49.490
Get down, Asirpa. Hide behind the sled.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:53.660
So they first aimed at the one 
carrying the three-shot gun.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:59.110
I'm lucky I swapped for the Berdan for 
a while, or that would've been me.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:03.720
They fired from a pretty long range.

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.700
That's an experienced sniper.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.020
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:20.590
Ammaa!

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.610
Ammaa!

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.840
Ammaa!

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:33.410
There he is.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.750
In that forest.

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.720
Ammaa!

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:50.160
Sure it's them?

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:56.250
An Uilta shouldn't be carrying 
the latest model of Japanese rifle.

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:59.290
Did we hit the guy on the warrant?

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:00.290
No way to know.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:07.300
Don't let any of them go. 
If they resist, kill them all.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.910
Who are they?

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:09.950
Robbers?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:13.940
I saw the barrel of a Mosin–Nagant 
poking out from one of those trees.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:16.120
Russian border guards, no doubt.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:20.210
Maybe they saw the three-shot Japanese gun
 and thought something was wrong.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.200
But that doesn't explain 
why they'd just open fire.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:25.850
Shiraishi, run and pick up my gun.

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:26.960
Hell no!

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.300
Shiraishi, drive the sled forward!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.720
We'll hide in that forest!

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:32.720
Come on...

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:37.290
They know we're trying to hide in the forest!

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.370
We have to go anyway!

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:38.980
Do it!

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:41.150
Go! Go!

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:43.520
Damn it!

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.110
I've never heard of border guards in Karafuto

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:50.240
just opening fire on somebody 
for crossing the border.

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.200
So you're saying it's an ambush?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.200
Ammaa!

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:57.360
Ammaa!

00:14:58.460 --> 00:14:59.870
Ammaa...

00:15:00.610 --> 00:15:01.920
Ammaa...

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.940
Ammaa...

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:19.890
Kiroranke Nispa?

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:40.810
Fire, Vasili!

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.210
Fire now!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:04.810
Now! Go!

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:08.230
Go! Go! Go!

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:24.840
I can see to the bone, but it 
didn't pass through the head.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:27.580
The big hat helped deflect it.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:30.850
I'm glad he ain't dead,

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:33.930
but, Kiro-chan, that was still crazy.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:35.210
What got into you?

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:37.440
You could've been shot!

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:42.930
Kamuy renkayne.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.060
It's thanks to the kamuy.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.130
No, it's thanks to me.

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:51.600
And the old guy's life was saved by his hat.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:54.570
Everything that happens has a reason...

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:58.660
Including our current predicament.

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.650
Saving him was the right thing to do.

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:03.500
But that was reckless.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:07.400
Did you have a reason, Kiroranke Nispa?

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.210
We'll ask them personally.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:17.750
Time for round two of the Russo-Japanese War.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:27.810
Vasili! Where are you going? He's badly hurt!

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.770
We're letting the man who 
killed the emperor escape.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:35.050
That's right. Kill him and 
we can get a promotion.

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.870
We won't have to spend every day 
hunting squirrels to kill time.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:43.950
The man who shot Ilya 
could've aimed for the head.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:49.600
He shot the stomach to slow us down,
 give them time to escape.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:54.300
Go after them!

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:10.020
<i>Even if a comrade's been shot,</i>

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:13.500
<i>if you let your emotions take over, 
you're not fit to be a sniper.</i>

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:21.240
<i>A good sniper is cold, interested most
 in murder and pursuing his prey.</i>

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:25.590
<i>They can't get far through this 
thick forest on reindeer.</i>

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.500
<i>They know they can't get away from us.</i>

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:31.480
<i>If it were me...</i>

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:35.460
<i>If I were the man who'd attacked Ilya,</i>

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:39.050
<i>I'd wait for the enemy to find 
the tracks left by my sled,</i>

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:42.970
<i>and set an ambush when they followed.</i>

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:55.110
<i>If I go around from the side,</i>

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.320
<i>I should be able to see where 
from the slope they fire.</i>

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:05.520
<i>Now shoot. Take the bait.</i>

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:11.440
<i>What's wrong? Why don't you shoot?</i>

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:17.660
<i>Oh. If I were him, I'd be waiting for me.</i>

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:25.050
<i>The ones who are cut out to be snipers 
are so careful, they're almost cowardly.</i>

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.520
<i>He wouldn't just come out and show himself.</i>

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.270
What is this?

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:37.980
It works more or less the same as a match.

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.290
Stab a roughly-filed stick 
of metal into gunpowder.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.720
When it's lifted up, it'll spark.

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:50.740
<i>A bomb trap.</i>

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:53.830
<i>It must be the regicide who set it.</i>

00:19:55.740 --> 00:19:57.410
<i>That man, perhaps?</i>

00:19:57.920 --> 00:19:59.440
<i>Should I have shot him?</i>

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:03.500
<i>I was showing respect to his willingness 
to risk his life for comrade.</i>

00:20:04.310 --> 00:20:05.470
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:20:07.370 --> 00:20:10.330
<i>I didn't like the way he seemed 
to be saying, "Go ahead and shoot."</i>

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:15.020
<i>I'm the sniper. I decide when you die.</i>

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:21.480
<i>Yeah. You wouldn't reveal 
yourself to go save them.</i>

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:26.700
<i>You could listen to these 
screams all night and not care.</i>

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.590
Yulbars!

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.470
Yulbars!

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:45.060
What does he keep saying?

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:50.200
Yulbars!

00:20:56.390 --> 00:20:57.860
Yulbars...

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:02.240
Russia has not forgotten you!

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:13.150
<i>I found him.</i>

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:24.240
<i>Even firing a single shot will 
be enough to tell him where I am.</i>

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:28.580
<i>When I fire, I have to kill him.</i>

00:21:29.700 --> 00:21:34.000
<i>If I don't, I'll be the next to be shot.</i>

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:56.680
<i>That's strange.</i>

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.280
<i>He's not moving at all...</i>

00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Bad Sign</b>

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:39.640
Next Time: "Bad Sign."
